      "line": 1128,
      "evidence": "The new deleted-target flow accepts a base-verified regular file, then sends its path to a danger-full-access dispatch where Codex can read its prior contents from Git history. The whole-repository secret scan walks current disk contents and skips .git; the added deleted-target check only rejects sensitive basenames. A deleted file with a neutral name but a credential in its contents therefore bypasses both checks and becomes available to the unsandboxed review.",
